<title>JAPAN: NCB sees 1st half 97/98 oper profit above Y35 bln.</title>
<headline>NCB sees 1st half 97/98 oper profit above Y35 bln.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nippon Credit Bank Ltd (NCB) expects its operating profit in the first half of 1997/98 to surpass 35 billion yen, NCB chairman Hiroshi Kubota told a news conference on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The new conference was held to announce the appointment of vice president Shigeoki Togo as NCB's new president. Togo is scheduled to assume the bank's presidency on August 19.</p>
<p>Togo told the same news conference that the bank would try to improve its credit rating and reduce fund-raising costs.</p>
</text>
